MID_EV12_008_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_008_m01_001: So your ship was wrecked by a huge sea beast, and\nyou washed up in Dagda. Have I got that right?
MID_EV12_008_m01_002: And now, since you're basically adrift, you're\nheading to Dagsion for the Heroic Games.
MID_EV12_008_m01_003: Good thing this all happened! Otherwise I'd be in\nthe belly of a sea beast by now.
MID_EV12_008_m01_004: I also got to avenge my dad. The stars really aligned\nfor us, didn't they? Drawn together by fate!
MID_EV12_008_m01_005: Having said all that... Tell me, mystery man. What's\nyour name?
MID_EV12_008_m01_006: Dietrich. Dietrich Gregor Lamine.
MID_EV12_008_m01_007: Now that's a complicated name. What's the\nlast part mean? "Lamine"?
MID_EV12_008_m01_008: Lamine is a great ancestor of mine. It has been the\nname of my house for generations.
MID_EV12_008_m01_009: Your house has a name? Fancy! Just like a king!
MID_EV12_008_m01_010: These Fódlan names are real tongue twisters. I think\nI'll just call you Sweetie.
MID_EV12_008_m01_011: Sweetie?
MID_EV12_008_m01_012: Aren't you going to ask me why I came to the\nempire of Dagda?
MID_EV12_008_m01_013: Oh...you? No. I don't care. In fact, I'm not interested\nin you at all.
MID_EV12_008_m01_014: Impudent beast...
MID_EV12_008_m01_015: Hm? Something to say?
MID_EV12_008_m01_016: Looks like something's on your mind.
MID_EV12_008_m01_017: <NCA>Mention the beasts at the reef.
MID_EV12_008_m01_018: <NCB>Mention the monster that attacked the ship.
MID_EV12_008_m01_019: <ACA>Those beasts at the reef were unlike the one that\nattacked my ship.
MID_EV12_008_m01_020: <ACA>So you say. And on the ship, Answerer's blade\nrang out...
MID_EV12_008_m01_021: <ACA>My supposition is that two Crest Stones resonated.
MID_EV12_008_m01_022: <ACA>This happens when one with a Hero's Relic draws\nnear to a dragon.
MID_EV12_008_m01_023: <ACB>The monster that attacked the ship was marked with\nthe Crest of Blaiddyd.
MID_EV12_008_m01_024: <ACB>Are you saying it was a remnant of the dragons that\nonce ruled Fódlan?
MID_EV12_008_m01_025: <ACB>{SetColor=Gray}Wait a moment... The Crest of Blaiddyd? Surely not.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_008_m01_026: <ACB>What? What are you looking at me for?
MID_EV12_008_m01_027: <ACB>Oh, no reason.
MID_EV12_008_m01_028: What matters now is that you want to defeat that\nsea monster yourself. Right, Sweetie?
MID_EV12_008_m01_029: Indeed. It is imperative that I face it again. I must\ncull it with this blade.
MID_EV12_008_m01_030: You know, you've got me thinking. If this monster\nreally is so much stronger than Redears...
MID_EV12_008_m01_031: Maybe it's not just some sea beast. Maybe it's\nCetus, the Sea Tyrant.
MID_EV12_008_m01_032: You know it? Tell me.
MID_EV12_008_m01_033: Well, I don't know a lot. But I know someone who\ndoes! He's called Tsiskaridze.
MID_EV12_008_m01_034: A weird old guy who lives in the village...he's pretty\nwise, actually, and he told me about Cetus.
MID_EV12_008_m01_035: Fact is, Cetus is all he ever wants to talk about, day\nin, day out. People kinda got tired of hearing it.
MID_EV12_008_m01_036: I'll show you where he lives! No time like\nthe present. Let's go!
MID_EV12_009_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_009_m01_001: Oh! You want to hear about Cetus, the Sea\nTyrant? 
MID_EV12_009_m01_002: Yeah, just tell them what you told me. Keep it\nsnappy.
MID_EV12_009_m01_003: Hmm...
MID_EV12_009_m01_004: Cetus, Tyrant of the Sea... As you might expect,\nno stronger creature swims the Lir Sea.
MID_EV12_009_m01_005: It lives in a raging storm and will gulp down other\nsea beasts whole, headfirst!
MID_EV12_009_m01_006: People thought it was just a legend... But lately, it's\nbeen sighted often.
MID_EV12_009_m01_007: Now the Lir Sea is much more dangerous. Even\nthe greediest merchants think twice before sailing.
MID_EV12_009_m01_008: <NCA>Ask about its size.
MID_EV12_009_m01_009: <NCB>Ask about its speed.
MID_EV12_009_m01_010: <ACA>Tell me, how large is this Cetus?
MID_EV12_009_m01_011: <ACA>Enormous! The sea beasts around here don't even\nbegin to compare.
MID_EV12_009_m01_012: <ACA>It brings the storm, eyes burning like fire... Once\nit rams into a ship, that ship is sunk!
MID_EV12_009_m01_013: <ACB>Tell me, how fast is this Sea Tyrant?
MID_EV12_009_m01_014: <ACB>Extraordinarily so! It's the fastest thing beneath\nthe waves.
MID_EV12_009_m01_015: <ACB>Doesn't matter how quick your ship is—you won't\noutrun it. If it catches sight of you, you're done for.
MID_EV12_009_m01_016: There can be no doubt. It was Cetus. I must fight it.\nHow can I bring this to pass?
MID_EV12_009_m01_017: Well, you can't take just any ship out. Cetus will\nsmash the hull to bits, and you'll be fish food.
MID_EV12_009_m01_018: However... Yes. A ship made of guibouga\nmight work.
MID_EV12_009_m01_019: That is unfamiliar to me. Is it of this land?
MID_EV12_009_m01_020: It's a type of wood so sturdy it's uncanny. But there's\nnot much of it left. All been cut down.
MID_EV12_009_m01_021: You'll see it at market now and again, but it costs a\nransom. It's truly worth its weight in gold.
MID_EV12_009_m01_022: Guibouga, guibouga... Oh, yes! There's an old tale\nthat Dagda the Great built a hundred warships of it...
MID_EV12_009_m01_023: Funny thing is, there are no records they ever\nlaunched. Perhaps they are still in Dagsion.
MID_EV12_009_m01_024: Guibouga doesn't rot, so if they still exist...you could\nsail them to this day.
MID_EV12_009_m01_025: Sweetie? I have a great idea.
MID_EV12_009_m01_026: We're going to Dagsion! We'll win the Heroic\nGames and get a warship as our prize!
MID_EV12_009_m01_027: After all, they're not even using them! There's no\nway they'll say no to giving us just one little ship.
MID_EV12_009_m01_028: You want to fight in the games, and you also want\nto slay the Sea Tyrant. It's a flawless plan!
MID_EV12_009_m01_029: You are correct. We will do as you say.
MID_EV12_009_m01_030: You want to fight in the Heroic Games? They're all\nthe way in Dagsion! You'd better get a move on.
MID_EV12_009_m01_031: It's almost Maresh! The games are starting soon. If\nyou want to participate, you need to get there quick.
MID_EV12_009_m01_032: That settles it! Time to hit the road...to Dagsion!
MID_EV12_100_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_100_m01_001: As we travel, should you not be more discreet with\nyour weapon?
MID_EV12_100_m01_002: Explain yourself.
MID_EV12_100_m01_003: Heroes' Relics are Fódlan's weapons for slaying\ndragons. Dragons are the gods of this world.
MID_EV12_100_m01_004: The gods of Dagda will see your weapon as a\nprovocation. They will not be pleased.
MID_EV12_100_m01_005: In the interest of safety, would it not be better to\nconceal it until it is truly needed?
MID_EV12_100_m01_006: Any who stand in my way will be disposed of. That\nis all.
MID_EV12_100_m01_007: Of course. Suggesting otherwise was my error.
MID_EV12_100_m01_008: Realization dawns upon me... You do not merely find\ntrouble, you seek it.
MID_EV12_100_m01_009: {SetColor=Gray}And here I am, tasked with a critical mission by the\nidealistic serpent that watches the world...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_100_m01_010: {SetColor=Gray}Yet I find myself drawn to your feral beauty. Things\nmay get out of hand, thanks to you.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_100_m01_011: What is it?
MID_EV12_100_m01_012: Nothing significant. I have simply come to realize\nthat, traveling with you, I need not fear boredom.
MID_EV12_100_m01_013: Sweetie? This guy Fabio? He is really, really weird.
MID_EV12_100_m01_014: Are all the priests of Fódlan like this?
MID_EV12_100_m01_015: I feel that his concept of the divine differs greatly\nfrom that which the church espouses.
MID_EV12_100_m01_016: He does not see the gods as the guides of the\npeople—that much is clear.
MID_EV12_100_m01_017: Strangely, though, I suspect that he and I may be\nin accord.
MID_EV12_010_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_010_m01_001: Here we are. It is as I suspected.
MID_EV12_010_m01_002: This is a weird door. Why is it here?
MID_EV12_010_m01_003: Well, whatever—I can open it. Sweetie, stand back.
MID_EV12_010_m01_004: Hnnng... Uh...what?
MID_EV12_010_m01_005: It didn't even budge! Not even a little bit! Well, I\nguess this is as far as we go.
MID_EV12_010_m01_006: What you are doing is futile. Step aside.
MID_EV12_010_m01_007: Yes, you can use your Crest to bolster your strength.\nBut in this world, there are proper ways to do things.
MID_EV12_010_m01_008: Foolhardy to think a blast door like this could simply\nbe shoved open by hand.
MID_EV12_010_m01_009: Hm...
MID_EV12_010_m01_010: It opened? No way! What's going on here?
MID_EV12_010_m01_011: It is time we meet the Grand Oracle—one who has\nlong watched over this land.
MID_EV12_011_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_011_m01_001: Now then... Allow me.
MID_EV12_011_m01_002: Grand Megalith! Heed my call.
MID_EV12_011_m01_003: Hmm.
MID_EV12_011_m01_004: You, who would consult with one of Kunlun. State\nyour name.
MID_EV12_011_m01_005: Kunlun? I am unaware of the group of which\nyou speak.
MID_EV12_011_m01_006: I am Fa—no. I am Anacharsis of Agartha. My rank\nis Adept. I have been dispatched from Shambhala.
MID_EV12_011_m01_007: O Grand Oracle Katarina, I have come to entreat\nyour aid.
MID_EV12_011_m01_008: Speak, Anacharsis. Explain Shambhala.
MID_EV12_011_m01_009: EX-017. A large subterranean structure built to house\nOracle Fermi, the Grand Megalith.
MID_EV12_011_m01_010: Speak, Anacharsis. Explain Agartha.
MID_EV12_011_m01_011: An offshoot of the Alliance of the Great Acolytes of\nRecondite Technology and Harmonic Alignment.
MID_EV12_011_m01_012: We Agarthans made Shambhala our base. Our\nobjective: to reclaim the surface from the beasts.
MID_EV12_011_m01_013: We are a collective of noble intellects revived since\nthe Great Undoing. This world is rightfully ours.
MID_EV12_011_m01_014: We, under the leadership of the prophet Thales, will\nexecute the plan devised by Vritra.
MID_EV12_011_m01_015: Ah! What? No!
MID_EV12_011_m01_016: Fabio? What the hell is going on? What did you do?
MID_EV12_011_m01_017: Kunlun has a prohibition against negotiating with\naffiliates of Vritra.
MID_EV12_011_m01_018: Eliminate the intruders. Eliminate the intruders.
MID_EV12_011_m01_019: I am deeply sorry. It appears I have failed.
MID_EV12_011_m01_020: Yeah, I noticed! "Allow me," he says, and this is how\nthings end up!
MID_EV12_011_m01_021: And here I thought that meant you could handle it!\nNow what?
MID_EV12_011_m01_022: It is no matter. It seems I need not fear boredom\nwith you around.
MID_EV12_011_m01_023: Phantoms shrouded by lightning. Interesting... Let\nme discover how it feels to cleave through them!
MID_EV12_063_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_063_m01_001: Why do you defend him?! Are you with Vritra too?
MID_EV12_063_m01_002: Whew...
MID_EV12_063_m01_003: Katarina, those are the enemy's reinforcements.\nEradicate them immediately!
MID_EV12_063_m01_004: Attack request denied.
MID_EV12_063_m01_005: Why?! Are they... Are they not with Vritra, then?
MID_EV12_063_m01_006: Who are they? If they are not with Vritra, perhaps\nthey are from Kunlun.
MID_EV12_063_m01_007: Yet I do not recognize them... Nor have I heard\nabout any of them from Zenon.
MID_EV12_063_m01_008: Could it be the Mediator Sicyon?
MID_EV12_063_m01_009: The second Mediator—the very one who betrayed\nKunlun and deserted us. But then...
MID_EV12_063_m01_010: Master Long, do you know who this is?
MID_EV12_063_m01_011: I cannot be certain. Perhaps it's... No, no. Something\nfeels strange here.
MID_EV12_063_m01_012: Have you forgotten? The battle continues.
MID_EV12_063_m01_013: Tch...
MID_EV12_063_m01_014: Hmm.
MID_EV12_063_m01_015: Stop! You can't touch that! What are you doing?
MID_EV12_012_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_012_m01_001: Everything up until now... Don't tell me it was all a\ndream? What in the world just happened?
MID_EV12_012_m01_002: No. We conversed with the Grand Oracle, were met\nwith force, and thence bathed in white light.
MID_EV12_012_m01_003: Everything we experienced just now was\nunmistakably real.
MID_EV12_012_m01_004: And it was also a failure, it seems. Compounded,\neven, by the interruption from interlopers.
MID_EV12_012_m01_005: The martyr's unshakable conviction took the form of\nan ardent defense. Yet still, we failed very badly.
MID_EV12_012_m01_006: Once again, it seems I have gleaned\nnothing whatsoever.
MID_EV12_012_m01_007: <NCA>Ask about what's going on.
MID_EV12_012_m01_008: <NCB>Ask about the intruders.
MID_EV12_012_m01_009: <ACA>What exactly is going on?
MID_EV12_012_m01_010: <ACA>The megalith with the personality called Katarina\nwas originally ours.
MID_EV12_012_m01_011: <ACA>Yet she did not see me as an ally at all. Nor did\nthose interlopers who appeared.
MID_EV12_012_m01_012: <ACA>You serve the Church of Seiros, do you not? Is that\nwho you mean by "ours"?
MID_EV12_012_m01_013: <ACA>Well... Let us just say that I shall explain everything\nat a more opportune time.
MID_EV12_012_m01_014: <ACB>Did you know those people?
MID_EV12_012_m01_015: <ACB>No. I'd never met any of them. Yet they showed an\nunmistakable animosity toward me, didn't they?
MID_EV12_012_m01_016: <ACB>I observed enough to have an educated guess as to\nwho they might be.
MID_EV12_012_m01_017: <ACB>I will explain all that in time. If we continue this\njourney, we will surely encounter them again.
MID_EV12_012_m01_018: <ACB>The one clad in white who appeared at the last, to\nend the fight... We encountered them before.
MID_EV12_012_m01_019: <ACB>Their identity is a mystery to me. But they appeared\nto defend you.
MID_EV12_012_m01_020: More importantly, though, I led you on a useless\ndetour. For that, you have my apologies.
MID_EV12_012_m01_021: There is no problem. My heart clamored when we\nfought those people. I would fight them again.
MID_EV12_012_m01_022: Hmm... I want to hear about this Grand Megalith.\nHow long has that been around?
MID_EV12_012_m01_023: Let me consider... At a minimum, it would be\nere the gods of Dagda claimed this land.
MID_EV12_012_m01_024: Yes, a far longer span than you could imagine. It has\nendured for age upon age.
MID_EV12_012_m01_025: It didn't look that old to me... Just who are\nyou, anyway?
MID_EV12_012_m01_026: I suspect the ones we encountered underground\nhave themselves survived the ages.
MID_EV12_012_m01_027: {SetColor=Gray}"Kunlun"? The holy mountains? Do they pretend they\nhave descended from the home of the celestials?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_012_m01_028: Oh? Strange. You may find its nature surprising, but\nknow that we have encountered another problem.
MID_EV12_012_m01_029: The shift we experienced was not just in space, but\nin time as well. One week has elapsed.
MID_EV12_012_m01_030: Elapsed since what? I don't get it.
MID_EV12_012_m01_031: I hesitate to say it... But I do surmise, given this\nnewly discovered circumstance...
MID_EV12_012_m01_032: We will be quite unable to make it in time to register\nfor the Heroic Games.
MID_EV12_012_m01_033: The ancient folktales of the far east told of decades\nspent within dreams that lasted but a moment.
MID_EV12_012_m01_034: Our present situation seems similar. Though I would\nthat it were all a dream...
MID_EV12_012_m01_035: What? Why are you so calm? This is not good!